  SIGNIFICANCE OF SEASONALITY
  ---------------------------

    Significance of seasonality is assessed using the variances of the
    total estimation error, which includes the error in the preliminary estimator
    (the revision error) and the error in the final estimator.
    Because the S.E. of the seasonal component estimator varies (it reaches a minimum
    for historical estimation and a maximum for the most distant forecast), the significance of seasonality
    will be different for different periods.
    An extreme example would be a series showing significant seasonality for historical estimates,
    that is poorly captured concurrently, and useless for forecasting.


        SEASONAL                      NUMBER OF PERIODS IN A YEAR THAT
        COMPONENT                     HAVE SIGNIFICANT SEASONALITY
